 EVIDENCE_INTEGRITY_BREACH added to NO_RETRY_REASONS (additive - no existing reason is redefined); a nullable `failure_reason` property on the gate objects the two non-retriable conditions produce (evalConsensus's blocking-dissent FAIL branch emits ADVOCATE_DISSENT; evalSkillsClean's two integrity FAIL branches emit EVIDENCE_INTEGRITY_BREACH) so the reason is a field rather than a substring of `detail`; and two additive top-level report fields - `terminal_failure_reason` (first non-null gate reason in a documented precedence order, else run_manifest.failure_reason) and `failure_severity` (that reason's severity via the helper). Exports gain `failureReasonSeverity` and `TERMINAL_FAILURE_REASON_PRECEDENCE`.\n\n2. references/ becomes the authoritative, severity-bearing table. phase-gates.md's prose class lists are replaced by ONE canonical table with a row per reason and a Severity column (plus an in-run 'no-retry' column, because PROTECTED_BRANCH_BLOCKED is no-retry yet classified retriable by the script - the two axes must not be conflated), immediately followed by the reason-selection precedence rule that makes ADVOCATE_DISSENT and EVIDENCE_INTEGRITY_BREACH beat the {PHASE}_GATE_FAILURE fallback, and by the sourcing rule (read severity from execution_report.json, never from gate detail prose). artifact-layout.md pins run_manifest.failure_reason as a closed enum owned by that table and documents the new report fields (append-only rule 8 makes an undocumented extra key schema drift, so this is required, not cosmetic). validator-inputs.md's execution-report.js rows carry the same sourcing rule where an orchestrator actually looks up the script.\n\nDeliberate boundaries. No new reference FILE: scripts/local-ci/frontmatter-lint.mjs enforces a BIDIRECTIONAL index (every references/*.md must be named in SKILL.md), and SKILL.md is outside allowed_paths - so a new file would fail Tier-1 CI with no in-scope fix. SCHEMA_VERSION stays '1.4.0': parity/execution-report-fixtures/run-tests.js line 444 asserts it exactly and parity/ is a blocked path, so a bump the file's own additive-change convention would suggest cannot be paired with its fixture update in this job; the builder records that deferral as a comment beside SCHEMA_VERSION where a reviewer reads it. No routing change for any existing reason (constraint 2), no new gate key, no decision/exit-code vocabulary change (non-goal 1), no fixture edits - the corpus keeps scoring the same decision and exit code because no fixture records either affected token in run_manifest and the new fields are additive keys the runner never compares.\n\nOut-of-scope consequence the operator must decide on (NOT planned, because the file is outside allowed_paths): adws-pipeline/skill-manifest.json is a content digest of every shipped file under adws-pipeline/, and scripts/local-ci/skill-manifest.mjs fails the Tier-1 gate when it is stale. Editing four shipped files without regenerating it makes `make local-ci` red on the skill-manifest step alone. See phase_log.md.",
